the gameplay premiere for hyrule  warriors age of calamity happened at  tokyo game show 2020. along with a new  trailer and some info from the  developers we've picked out a few  details that you might have missed  here are 8 things we learned from hyrule  warriors age of calamity tokyo game  shows showcase  breath of the wild is the sole focus of  this game the original hyrule warriors  was a celebration of all things zelda  with characters and locations from  multiple games in the series  in this game however its sole focus is  the world and characters of breath of  the wild  so don't count zelda characters from the  entire timeline to show up  age of calamity takes place 100 years  before the events of birth of the wild  in the period shown through the memories  unlocked in the game  so this time koei tecmo worked more  closely with the zelda development team  on gameplay  characters and the depiction of hyrule  if you played the original hyrule  warriors you'll feel right at home  with age of calamity you'll gain a  special attack after defeating a certain  amount of enemies  have the ability to switch characters  mid battle use attack to combo skill  trees and acquire crafting materials for  upgrades  all things that will feel familiar if  you played the first hyrule warriors  after watching this recent gameplay we  suggest that if you want to get a leg up  in age of calamity  playing the original hyrule warriors is  a good way to get some practice in  beforehand  some interesting combat things link will  have access to the shortcut menu by  holding  r then pressing x y a or b which gives  them chica slate abilities courtesy of  our new little guardian friend  the interesting part is that in the  newly released trailer daruk is also  seen using stasis as well  meaning that this companion may possibly  be passed around to different champions  to let them all use sheikah slate  abilities  impa is also seen here using a seal  system numbered in the corner in chica  writing as letters  f s and t most likely first second and  third seals  letting her access another layer of  clones on each side of her and giving  her larger attacks  we got to see more of the little  guardian but it's still a mystery  first seen on the promotional art for  age of calamity the little guardian is  largely still a mystery  but we did get to see it up close it  looks like the sheikah slate awakened it  causing it to make the shika tower  appear  and it follows link around during combat  it's also seen following the main  characters around during cutscenes  what's its purpose we don't know is it  cute  heck yeah it is impa might not be the  only  new playable shika character impo was  revealed to be a new playable character  in age of calamity this makes sense that  she was one of the characters she  encountered in breath of the wild who  was alive during the attack 100 years  prior  but according to a rough translation  impa reportedly mentions pura pura is  impu's older sister who experimented  with an anti-aging rune  and became the young looking woman that  we see in breath of the wild is pura  going to be a playable character too  it's not entirely out of the realm of  possibility for a warriors game  other minor characters are also  confirmed to make an appearance while  it's unclear if any of these characters  are playable  we did see some minor characters from  breath of the wild make an appearance in  the new age of calamity trailer  this includes young sidon who was first  introduced in the champions ballot dlc  for breath of the wild  king dorfian who is mifa and sidon's  father and the great deku tree  fighting as a great deku tree sounds  like a lot of fun but it's probably too  overpowered  the game will be dubbed in english  during the stream nintendo released a  new trailer on their english channels  which revealed that the game will be  dubbed  at least the cutscenes will there was  some dialogue heard in the original  trailer but it was the same reused voice  lines from breath of the wild  it's unclear at this time whether  everyone in the original cast is  returning  but this is a welcome change from the  original hyrule warriors which just had  grunts during cut scenes as text was  appearing  only japan is getting the cool edition  during the panel we got a closer look at  the treasure box edition of age of  calamity which includes goodies like an  acrylic art plate a metal guardian charm  and a blanket design like link's  parasail unfortunately this edition was  said to be only coming to japan  and will not come overseas thankfully  the nintendo switch is region free so  feel free to try and order anyways  although quantities are limited and some  retailers already went live  and that's it age of calamity is less  than two months away at this point so  it's not much longer before we get our  hands on it wouldn't it be nice to not  have it come out on the day after  cyberpunk 2077  sure but we can't always get what we  want if you're looking for the full  gameplay sequence from the stream or the  entire stream itself  head over to our youtube channel and for  more age of calamity coverage and  everything zelda stay tuned to gamespot  you
 

